Find $\theta$ to the nearest degree, given that it is obtuse.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (1.9662,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.2381,2.2535);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,above left] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,below right] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\pic[draw,angle radius=7mm,angle eccentricity=1.5,"$28^{\circ}$"] {angle=B--A--C};
\pic[draw,angle radius=5mm,angle eccentricity=1.5,"$\theta$"] {angle=C--B--A};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The two triangles shown have a $24^{\circ}$ angle, a $15$ cm side and a $9$ cm side. Find both possible sizes of the angle opposite the $15$ cm side, to the nearest degree.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.3850,1.9523);
\coordinate (P) at (2.2678,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (6.5023,0);
\draw (A)--(Q)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (C)--(P);
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,above left] {$15\text{ cm}$};
\path (C)--(P) node[midway,left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\path (C)--(Q) node[midway,above right] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\pic[draw,angle radius=8mm,angle eccentricity=1.5,"$24^{\circ}$"] {angle=Q--A--C};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below] at (P) {$P$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[above] at (C) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
